      "summary": {
        "unit_id": "hmh07-lua-follow6:178",
        "answer": "Takes a controller. Returns false for the PC/platform-native predicate, then false for non-PC Russian. In the final else block declares local f64_local0. Outside a game, an offline-demo branch queries hash_5CB675CA7856DA25 and returns its falsy value early; otherwise evaluates IsERegEnabled and, only if truthy, issignedintodemonware. In-game sets the block-local variable false. After that entire else block ends, line 1052 returns the separate non-local f64_local0, not the ended block-local variable. Preserve that literal scoping defect; the intended normal result is not reconstructed or silently repaired.",
        "unknowns": [
          "Effective HMH settings/data/assets, true load/overwrite/class lookup order, original recovered-text fidelity, native callback delivery and service/server implementations remain open.",
          "Independent correctness review and final game tests remain deferred.",
          "The final f64_local0 read is outside the else block containing its local declaration. Whole-file and exact-fragment ASTs classify line1052 as a non-local identifier. Intended normal return needs original fidelity/VM evidence; no repair."
        ],
